NAME
    wmfiles - tiny file-manager WM client (Path C phase 21)

SYNOPSIS
    wmfiles [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Open a 400x300 window showing the entries in the current
    working directory.  Click a row to select it, or use the
    arrow keys (after click-focusing wmfiles so it receives the
    keyboard stream).

    Keyboard (focus required):
      Up / Down arrow   move the selection
      Enter             cd into the selected entry (if a dir)
      Backspace         cd ..
      r / R             reload the entry list
      q / Q / Esc       close the window

    Arrow keys arrive as the standard ANSI CSI sequences
    ESC '[' 'A'/'B'/'C'/'D'; wmfiles parses them with a tiny
    state machine across consecutive WM_EV_KEY events.

    No scrollbar: an over-long directory listing just clips at
    the bottom of the window.  Reload (r) after creating new
    files outside wmfiles.

SEE ALSO
    wmd(1), wmtype(1)
